  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason—namely, the small probability difference (0.1 percentage points) and the comparison of maximum outcomes (6000 vs. 3000)—is explicitly considered by the individual. The individual treats the 0.1% difference as acceptable (i.e., negligible) and prefers the higher maximum outcome, which aligns with the rule of the decision reason. The justification in the verbal report ('0.1% Wahrscheinlichkeitsabweichung... machten... B attraktiver') directly mirrors the logic of the reason: accept a negligible probability reduction for a better maximum outcome. Therefore, both the information considered and the decision rule match the decision reason. There is strong evidence that the individual used this reason in their deliberation.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
}

